WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.849
Can you teach a language model a new skill by only deleting

00:00:03.849 --> 00:00:04.966
some of its weights?

00:00:04.966 --> 00:00:06.640
Or by solving a single equation?

00:00:10.665 --> 00:00:11.754
Hi, I'm Fennimore!

00:00:11.754 --> 00:00:16.112
Two ways to teach a language model a skill without ordinary fine-tuning.

00:00:16.112 --> 00:00:17.202
One deletes weights.

00:00:17.202 --> 00:00:19.017
The other solves one matrix.

00:00:20.717 --> 00:00:21.292
Chapter one.

00:00:21.292 --> 00:00:23.018
How a weight matrix can move.

00:00:27.442 --> 00:00:31.597
Every post-training method replaces a weight matrix with the matrix plus a change.

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:34.153
They differ in what that change may be.

00:00:34.573 --> 00:00:38.296
Full fine-tuning lets every entry move anywhere, by gradient descent.

00:00:38.716 --> 00:00:40.365
LoRA trains a low-rank update.

00:00:40.365 --> 00:00:43.994
Small to train, but merged in, every entry moves a little.

00:00:44.414 --> 00:00:48.440
A closed-form edit treats an MLP as a key-value store, and solves

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.782
for the change directly.

00:00:50.202 --> 00:00:53.463
And deletion: every changed entry goes to exactly zero.

00:00:53.463 --> 00:00:55.637
The only freedom is which ones.

00:00:56.967 --> 00:00:57.891
Chapter two.

00:00:57.891 --> 00:00:58.815
Deletion Tuning.

00:01:03.017 --> 00:01:06.952
Deletion Tuning keeps every pretrained weight, and learns only which gate weights

00:01:06.952 --> 00:01:08.264
to set to zero.

00:01:11.967 --> 00:01:13.384
Freeze a pretrained model.

00:01:13.384 --> 00:01:17.282
The target is one matrix per block, the MLP's gate projection.

00:01:17.702 --> 00:01:19.388
Every gate weight gets a logit.

00:01:19.388 --> 00:01:22.760
A steep sigmoid of it multiplies the weight, so the weight is

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:23.883
kept or nearly zero.

00:01:24.303 --> 00:01:29.387
The usual loss, from reinforcement learning or labels, sends gradients only to the logits.

00:01:29.387 --> 00:01:30.839
The weights never change.

00:01:31.259 --> 00:01:32.917
The sigmoid sharpens into a step.

00:01:32.917 --> 00:01:34.852
What ships is one bit per weight.

00:01:36.492 --> 00:01:38.508
Here is a toy gate matrix.

00:01:38.508 --> 00:01:40.189
The pretrained weights are frozen.

00:01:40.189 --> 00:01:43.885
Beside them, one trainable logit per weight, most just above zero.

00:01:44.305 --> 00:01:47.488
The layer uses each weight times a sigmoid of its logit.

00:01:47.488 --> 00:01:49.514
Early in training that mask is soft.

00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:53.578
The loss moves the logits, and the sharpness ramps up, until the

00:01:53.578 --> 00:01:54.793
sigmoid is a step.

00:01:54.793 --> 00:01:57.830
A logit that ends below zero has deleted its weight.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.319
What ships is one bit per weight.

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:01.797
The pretrained weights never changed.

00:02:04.092 --> 00:02:08.999
Llama three point two, one billion, has about two hundred sixty-eight million gate weights.

00:02:09.419 --> 00:02:11.540
The logits start from a pruning score.

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:13.964
The lowest-scoring sliver starts on the delete side.

00:02:14.384 --> 00:02:18.386
Random noise in the other logits puts about three hundred sixty-two thousand

00:02:18.386 --> 00:02:20.386
more below zero at step zero.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:23.819
The published mask deletes five hundred fifty-seven thousand.

00:02:23.819 --> 00:02:28.713
Under GRPO the count barely moves from where the starting values put it.

00:02:28.713 --> 00:02:30.595
Training chooses which bits flip.

00:02:32.342 --> 00:02:37.137
On Llama 3 8B under GRPO, it matches full fine-tuning: eighty-three point

00:02:37.137 --> 00:02:39.934
five five against eighty-three point two four.

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:41.932
The lead is four problems.

00:02:41.932 --> 00:02:42.731
A tie.

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:47.868
Forward KL from the base model, on the smallest Llama.

00:02:47.868 --> 00:02:51.608
The mask stays flat near zero while every other method climbs.

00:02:52.028 --> 00:02:53.592
Accuracy on six older tasks.

00:02:53.592 --> 00:02:57.659
The mask stays within a point of the base; the others drift down.

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:00.170
Chapter three.

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:01.577
One solve, no steps.

00:03:06.592 --> 00:03:10.130
A blog post from embedding dot in moves a teacher's decisions

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:11.417
into a small model.

00:03:11.417 --> 00:03:15.277
It edits the down projection of the MLP in the last layers.

00:03:15.697 --> 00:03:20.125
Only two hundred fifty-six neurons, the ones most active at the answer position.

00:03:20.545 --> 00:03:23.341
That is a block of two hundred sixty-two thousand weights.

00:03:23.761 --> 00:03:26.617
Found by one solve, in three point one milliseconds.

00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:29.191
Here is the formula.

00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:33.122
Keys are what the chosen neurons output at the answer.

00:03:33.122 --> 00:03:37.094
Values are how the final state must change to match a teacher's answer.

00:03:37.514 --> 00:03:41.084
This term protects ordinary text: it penalises any change in what

00:03:41.084 --> 00:03:42.383
the layer writes there.

00:03:42.803 --> 00:03:46.721
Set the gradient to zero, and the best edit is one linear solve.

00:03:46.721 --> 00:03:48.228
No steps, no learning rate.

00:03:49.842 --> 00:03:53.638
Drop the protection term, and the same solve still hits its targets.

00:03:53.638 --> 00:03:56.168
But perplexity goes to ten to the eleventh.

00:03:56.168 --> 00:03:58.066
The protection term is the method.

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:00.170
Chapter four.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:01.928
Read at their sample sizes.

00:04:05.567 --> 00:04:08.287
The article checked both posts against their own numbers.

00:04:08.707 --> 00:04:12.448
The edit post's eighteen percent baseline says no to everything.

00:04:12.448 --> 00:04:15.067
Always saying yes would score about eighty-two.

00:04:15.487 --> 00:04:19.777
Its damage check, one prompt hurt against five for LoRA, is fifteen prompts.

00:04:19.777 --> 00:04:21.096
Not yet a difference.

00:04:21.516 --> 00:04:25.769
And Deletion Tuning's fewer than zero point zero five percent holds for

00:04:25.769 --> 00:04:29.314
seven of eight GRPO masks, none of the supervised ones.

00:04:30.467 --> 00:04:34.164
And reworded, the same questions get five of eleven right from the

00:04:34.164 --> 00:04:36.320
edited model, eight from the unedited one.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:39.401
There is no sign the skill survives a new wording.

00:04:41.142 --> 00:04:43.213
Few changed weights is a side effect.

00:04:43.213 --> 00:04:47.059
Old skills survive when the edit is chosen by the task and anchored.

00:04:49.942 --> 00:04:52.168
Delete gate weights, or solve one matrix.

00:04:52.168 --> 00:04:55.030
Either way, check the baseline and the sample size.

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:55.984
Thanks for watching!

00:04:56.404 --> 00:04:58.558
Every source is in the full article.

00:04:58.558 --> 00:04:59.174
I'm Fennimore.

00:04:59.174 --> 00:04:59.482
Bye!
